From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wsclean-mx <wsclean-mx@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:57:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] Metal gridding: ducc0 kernel parameters, variant
 benchmark, cost attribution

The kernel now uses ducc0's form and parameters - K(v) = exp(beta*((1-v^2)^e0
- 1)) with beta = betaNorm*support, betaNorm = 2.10745629204644125 and e0 =
0.520621490478515692 from the W=6, ofactor=2.0, ndim=3, single-precision row
of their kernel database - replacing a naive beta = 2.3 variant whose edge
value exp(-2.3) ~ 0.1 left a 10% discontinuity at the support edge.

The probe now measures variants in one binary against the same float64 twin,
with a timing-only cost ablation:

  grid    nvis   analytic      hoisted      packed       costprobe  math share
  1024^2  200k   2.33 ms       3.49 (0.67x) 3.49 (0.67x) 1.63 ms    30%
  1024^2  1M     4.32 ms       6.71 (0.64x) 12.11 (0.36x) 2.86 ms   34%
  2048^2  2M     12.64 ms      15.72 (0.80x) 16.88 (0.75x) 6.65 ms  47%

Measured conclusions: the generic kernel is fastest (manual weight hoisting is
a deoptimization - the compiler already hoists, and the manual version costs
register pressure and fully unrolled 6x6 bodies); packing the bucket data does
not pay (it duplicates data per touched tile; 2.8x slower at 1M); kernel math
is 30-47% of the time, so the atomic/tile machinery is the next lever; and
linear interpolation tables cannot meet the accuracy requirement (normalized
weight error 2.0e-2 at oversample 2, 1.4e-3 at 8; tabulating the smooth part
g = (1-v^2)^e0 is worse, 4.3e-2, because g has an infinite derivative at the
support edge) - which is why ducc0 fits a polynomial and why the wiring stage
should port that polynomial rather than a naive table.

The kernel-accuracy check now judges absolute error in units of the kernel peak
plus relative error only where the kernel is significant (>= 1e-3 of peak),
because the ES kernel spans 1 to 3e-6 and float32 cannot represent the tail to
1e-6 relative; the bound is derived (dK/K = beta*dg ~ 3*beta*eps ~ 4.5e-6) and
the measured values are 1.5-2e-6. All variants stay within 4e-6 of the twin.

