+// Exponential-of-semicircle kernel in ducc0's form and parameters:
+//   K(v) = exp(beta * ((1-v^2)^e0 - 1)),  v = 2x/support,
+// with beta = betaNorm * support. The defaults are the W=6, ofactor=2.0,
+// ndim=3, single-precision row of ducc0's kernel database (epsilon 2.1e-5), so
+// the harness measures the same kernel shape the w-gridder uses.
+inline float es_kernel_ducc0(float x, float support, float beta, float e0) {
+  const float v = 2.0f * x / support;
+  const float tmp = 1.0f - v * v;
+  if (tmp < 0.0f) return 0.0f;
+  return exp(beta * (pow(tmp, e0) - 1.0f));
 }
 
-// The same kernel through the precise math namespace. Apple GPUs evaluate the
-// default exp/sqrt under fast math, which is not accurate enough for a strict
-// differential test against the CPU twin, so the gridding path uses this.
